WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.231 --> 00:00:01.064
- [Narrator] Fondue.

00:00:01.064 --> 00:00:03.294
It's this thing we do with cheese.

00:00:03.294 --> 00:00:04.153
We melt it.

00:00:04.153 --> 00:00:05.076
We dip it.

00:00:05.076 --> 00:00:06.133
We eat it.

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:08.573
In the '70s, it became super popular.

00:00:08.573 --> 00:00:10.927
But that didn't just happen by chance.

00:00:10.927 --> 00:00:13.197
There was an ominous force behind it,

00:00:13.197 --> 00:00:15.440
a real-life cheese cartel.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.190
(dramatic music)

00:00:20.005 --> 00:00:23.352
100 years ago, cheese was a
hot commodity in Switzerland.

00:00:23.352 --> 00:00:24.966
It was exported at high volumes

00:00:24.966 --> 00:00:27.671
and played a major role
in the Swiss economy.

00:00:27.671 --> 00:00:30.233
But that all changed after World War I.

00:00:30.233 --> 00:00:32.743
European countries, devastated by the war,

00:00:32.743 --> 00:00:35.926
could no longer afford to buy
expensive, imported cheese,

00:00:35.926 --> 00:00:38.600
which was bad news for Switzerland.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:40.037
So the government stepped in,

00:00:40.037 --> 00:00:42.673
and they formed The Cheese Union.

00:00:42.673 --> 00:00:44.575
Basically, it was a cartel,

00:00:44.575 --> 00:00:46.179
and it worked like this.

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:47.045
The first thing they did

00:00:47.045 --> 00:00:49.588
was force every dairy
farmer and cheesemonger

00:00:49.588 --> 00:00:53.009
to fix the price of cheese,
eliminating competition,

00:00:53.009 --> 00:00:55.388
meaning everyone could stay in the game.

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:57.067
The cheese cartel also told them

00:00:57.067 --> 00:01:01.063
exactly how much cheese to
make and limited the varieties.

00:01:01.063 --> 00:01:04.180
So instead of making thousands
of different kinds of cheese,

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:06.202
they only made seven.

00:01:06.202 --> 00:01:07.216
And it worked.

00:01:07.216 --> 00:01:11.266
The cartel controlled the
cheese supply for decades.

00:01:11.266 --> 00:01:13.033
By the '70s, they got greedy

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:15.944
and wanted to expand their
cheese racket globally.

00:01:15.944 --> 00:01:18.083
So they introduced the world to a dish

00:01:18.083 --> 00:01:22.368
already popular in the
freezing cold Alps, fondue.

00:01:22.368 --> 00:01:23.906
By marketing cheese for fondue,

00:01:23.906 --> 00:01:25.917
the cartel was able to sell more.

00:01:25.917 --> 00:01:26.851
I mean, think about it.

00:01:26.851 --> 00:01:30.192
It takes a lot, and I
mean a lot, of cheese

00:01:30.192 --> 00:01:31.762
to fill a pot.

00:01:31.762 --> 00:01:34.615
But, as with most
cartels, things got shady.

00:01:34.615 --> 00:01:35.743
Money went missing.

00:01:35.743 --> 00:01:36.959
People went to jail.

00:01:36.959 --> 00:01:41.074
And by the 1990s, the Swiss
Cheese Union was dismantled.

00:01:41.074 --> 00:01:42.267
So, there you have it.

00:01:42.267 --> 00:01:44.596
The reason we know and love fondue

00:01:44.596 --> 00:01:46.549
is because of a shady government program

00:01:46.549 --> 00:01:48.729
that convinced the world
to consume massive amounts

00:01:48.729 --> 00:01:50.146
of melted cheese.

